// Cross-lane word deskew. MUST be compiled BEFORE WavD2DGpio_v2.v below: this
// file `includes tidelink_sync_word.svh at $unit scope, which is what declares
// TIDELINK_SYNC_WORD / TIDELINK_SYNC_PERIOD for the parameter defaults of
// tidelink_phy_sync_insert / _detect. WavD2DGpio*.v also includes the header,
// but from INSIDE the module — so if it compiles first it sets the header's
// include guard while binding the constants to module scope, and the later
// $unit includes become no-ops (Error-[IND] identifier not declared). Same
// order as tidelink_fpga_v2.flist.
// F3c LOCAL OVERRIDE (2026-07-02): the deps copy is replaced by
// src/rtl/local_overrides/tidelink_lane_deskew_v2.sv — identical except the
// sync_hit idle-zero qualifier (lane-0 slice 0x1F00 popcount==TOL(5) made
// all-zero IDLE words continuously "match", starving the periodic confirm →
// sync_seen never commits on a quiet link). Submodule copy stays pristine, and
// the fix exists on no tidelink-phy branch, so this file is its only carrier.
// Keep in lockstep with tidelink_fpga_v2.flist — the ASIC build must not ship
// a deskew the FPGA link validation never ran.
// # Comment-out original: ${TIDELINK_HOME}/deps/tidelink-phy/rtl/tidelink_lane_deskew.sv
${TIDELINK_HOME}/src/rtl/local_overrides/tidelink_lane_deskew_v2.sv

// V2 PHY SWAP: serdes lane fork from the shared PHY component (FIX-N..R,
// silicon-validated 2026-06-10) replaces src/rtl/local_overrides/{WavD2DGpio,
// WavD2DGpioRx,WavD2DGpioTx}.v. Same module names — never co-compile with V1.
// R-A LOCAL OVERRIDE (2026-07-04): anchor-verify sticky (io_anchor_verified)
// — keep in lockstep with tidelink_fpga_v2.flist (local_overrides/Wlink.v
// connects the new port, so the deps copy would no longer elaborate here).
// # Comment-out original: ${TIDELINK_HOME}/deps/tidelink-phy/rtl/wav/WavD2DGpio.v
${TIDELINK_HOME}/src/rtl/local_overrides/WavD2DGpio_v2.v
// PHASE-B LOCAL OVERRIDE (2026-07-14): the deps WavD2DGpioRx.v is replaced by
// src/rtl/local_overrides/WavD2DGpioRx_v2.v — identical except the SHARED
// CAPTURE-CLOCK inputs (USE_EXT_CAP_CLK + io_cnt_clk_ext/io_cap_clk_ext), which
// let WavD2DGpio_v2 hoist the (lane-identical) capture mux chain out of the 8
// lanes and buffer it once, killing the fanout-372 general-routing capture-clock
// LUT behind the ~7 ns lane-7 clock skew. Must be kept in lockstep with
// WavD2DGpio_v2.v, which connects the two new ports — the deps copy would no
// longer elaborate here. Submodule copy stays pristine.
// SAFE FOR ASIC: USE_EXT_CAP_CLK defaults to 0 and WavD2DGpio_v2 derives
// USE_SHARED_CAP_BUFG from USE_CLKBUF, which is 0 on the ASIC flow ⇒ the shared
// chain + its 2 BUFGs are pruned and every lane keeps today's per-lane
// WavClockMux passthrough. Bit-identical to the deps copy in this flist.
// NOTE: distinct from src/rtl/local_overrides/WavD2DGpioRx.v (the V1 override,
// still owned by the V1 flists) — same module name, never co-compile.
// # Comment-out original: ${TIDELINK_HOME}/deps/tidelink-phy/rtl/wav/WavD2DGpioRx.v
${TIDELINK_HOME}/src/rtl/local_overrides/WavD2DGpioRx_v2.v
